@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 11, 17 and 16 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.35.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage/1.35.0> ; owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage/1.34.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1617corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.35.0 (2026-11-25): Chapter 17 page 9.23.0 built and tested: 416 checks passed, 0 failed. The first test of page 9.22.0 failed the main-thread budget (274 ms after load, limit 200); the budget was not changed. Cause found: a code box that receives about 40 lines at once ran the page-fit routine once per line (39 times, about 90 ms of forced layout). Fix: new template 9.54.1 runs it once per frame; same page data re-made as 9.23.0."""@en .

ex:TK10_Page_17_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done 2026-11-25. Page 9.23.0 built from template 9.54.1 (new file over 9.54.0, one line changed) and page data 9.23.0 (same chapter code manifest 1.2.0, lecture file from deck 4.0.0). The older page 9.22.0 stays in the folder, superseded." .
ex:TK10_Page_17_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done 2026-11-25. Full page test: 416 passed, 0 failed (log 08-tooling/ch17-page/logs_v9_23_0/page_test.log); story layout probe: pass at all three screen sizes (story_layout_probe.log); version check exit 0. The page 9.22.0 test had 414 passed and 2 failed, both the same main-thread budget check. NOT done: the generic code check (C1 to C5) was not run for chapter 17, because the tool reads a chapter source file with code as line lists, which chapter 17 does not have; the page test check P11 (page examples equal the deck code manifest) and the manifest self-check stand in for C1 to C3 and the page test runs every example for C4. Not looked at by eye: the page in a browser window, and the lecture tab text." .
ex:ST10_Page_17 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done 2026-11-25 on the checks above; the limits named in the Verify task apply. The owner has not yet read the page." .
